# Accounting agent: cron entries.
# deploy/install.sh --enable installs these between BEGIN/END marker lines in
# the user's crontab, with __HOME__ replaced by the repo path, and leaves every
# other line in that crontab alone. To install by hand instead:
#   sed "s|__HOME__|$PWD|g" deploy/crontab.example   then paste into `crontab -e`
#
# Times are UTC. If the server runs other jobs, keep these clear of them: a
# session competing for CPU or for the same Xero tenant runs slower and
# nearer the rate limit.
#
# Every Claude job goes through deploy/run-scheduled.sh, which holds the prompt,
# and then deploy/run-agent.sh, which takes the per-job lock, loads .env, defers
# the run if Xero is at its daily rate limit, commits any write-back and runs the
# phantom-payment check afterwards regardless of what the session thinks it did.

# --- daily Mon-Sat 02:00: the bookkeeping chain ----------------------------
# Three links one after another so two are never in Xero at once, each plain
# Python first (scripts/daily_chain.py) and a session only when there is work
# that needs judgement; a link skipped that way still runs its exit checks and
# posts its report to the channel at nil cost:
#   bookkeep  invoice intake from the Slack app and the accounting inbox, coded
#             and posted as AUTHORISED bills with the document attached, closed
#             with the bill-payments check. Everything stays unpaid; the bank
#             feed is still matched by hand in Xero.
#   interco   intercompany reconciliation, read-only, breaks and the journals
#             they need, plus the matrix workbook to Drive. Posts nothing. The
#             recon and the matrices run in Python first; a session starts
#             only for an open break, a verdict or an answer waiting, or a
#             revaluation ready.
#   ap-check  the open accounts payable position per entity from the bill feed,
#             overdue flagged, cross-checked against the bank feed. A session
#             starts only to post the legs for a new bill another entity's
#             bank paid.
# Sunday is excluded: the review takes that day.
0 2 * * 1-6 __HOME__/deploy/run-scheduled.sh daily >> __HOME__/data/logs/cron.log 2>&1

# --- Mon-Fri 02:00: bills payable report + unpaid list DM ------------------
# Fired at the same minute as the chain and waits on data/daily-chain.lock, so
# it runs the moment the bookkeeping has finished. scripts/bills_report.py,
# no Claude: every bill paid or open per entity, open bills searched for on
# the bank, one workbook to the Drive folder, then the UNPAID bills DM'd to
# [accounts_payable] unpaid_notify entity by entity.
0 2 * * 1-5 __HOME__/deploy/run-scheduled.sh bills >> __HOME__/data/logs/cron.log 2>&1

# --- Mon-Sat 02:00: prepayments, accruals, deposits, bank fees + summary ----
# The same days as the intercompany reconciliation in the chain. Fired at the
# same minute and waits on data/daily-chain.lock like `bills`, so it runs once
# the bookkeeping has finished and never alongside it. scripts/prepayments_report.py,
# accruals_report.py, deposits_report.py and bank_fees.py, no Claude: each refresh
# rebuilds its workbook under data/reports/ and publishes the copy to the Drive
# folder, then scripts/balance_reports_summary.py posts the findings to the
# channel. Read-only against Xero.
0 2 * * 1-6 __HOME__/deploy/run-scheduled.sh balance-reports >> __HOME__/data/logs/cron.log 2>&1

# --- Mon-Sat 02:00: the outstanding-items check ---------------------------
# Waits on data/daily-chain.lock like the two above and starts after them.
# scripts/outstanding_check.py: Python closes what Xero shows done, a
# read-only coordinator with checker agents judges the rest, and every line
# definitely done is deleted from the register. The run goes to the channel
# with its cost. [outstanding_check] in config/group.toml tunes or disables it.
0 2 * * 1-6 __HOME__/deploy/run-scheduled.sh outstanding-check >> __HOME__/data/logs/cron.log 2>&1

# --- Wed + Sun 10:00: full bookkeeping review ------------------------------
# Every entity in config/group.toml against docs/REVIEW_METHOD.md and rules/,
# plus the intercompany reconciliation the review skill requires as a
# standard check.
0 10 * * 0,3 __HOME__/deploy/run-scheduled.sh review >> __HOME__/data/logs/cron.log 2>&1

# --- optional, Mon 07:00: the outstanding-items list -----------------------
# Off by default (an admin asks for it in Slack). Uncomment to post the
# standing list to the channel every Monday.
# 0 7 * * 1 __HOME__/deploy/run-scheduled.sh outstanding >> __HOME__/data/logs/cron.log 2>&1

# --- Mon 07:00: weekly Claude usage report ---------------------------------
# scripts/usage_report.py, no Claude session: what every session cost by job
# against the week before, from the session JSON under data/runs/. A headline
# in the channel, the detail in its thread. Costs are notional on a
# subscription token.
0 7 * * 1 __HOME__/deploy/run-scheduled.sh usage >> __HOME__/data/logs/cron.log 2>&1

# --- every 10 minutes: Xero rate-limit retry sweep -------------------------
# A run that met the 5000-a-day Xero cap wrote data/retry/<job>.retry holding
# the second the cap resets. This re-runs it the moment that second passes.
*/10 * * * * __HOME__/deploy/retry-sweep.sh >> __HOME__/data/logs/retry-sweep.log 2>&1

# --- nightly: safety net (read-only, no Claude) ----------------------------
# Cheap independent check that nothing created a phantom payment today,
# including anything done by hand in Xero.
0 23 * * * cd __HOME__ && ./.venv/bin/python scripts/check_no_phantom_payments.py >> __HOME__/data/logs/phantom-check.log 2>&1

# --- weekly: log trim ------------------------------------------------------
# Logs older than 30 days under data/logs are deleted.
30 4 * * 0 find __HOME__/data/logs -type f -name '*.log' -mtime +30 -delete
